{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist","id":1545084,"title":"Concept for a Dark Ages story antagonist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-30T19:13:15-07:00","id":1545084,"title":"Concept for a Dark Ages story antagonist","content":"<br /> I recently thought of a concept for a Dark Ages antagonist. A Demon named Dia the Vine Queen who rules a Lust Cult in an isolated settlement in Scotland through fear, claiming she'll spare them during an alleged demonic invasion she claims will happen soon. She has a pack of Demonhounds in her service, a Demonic Boar, a Baali and a Black Spiral Dancer acting as her enforcers, a Succubus she created acting as a recruiter, some dumb villagers acting as her bodyguards and a pet Demonologist recruited from a monastery acting as her summoner whom she provided with an Imp familiar. For the rules I just use Dark Ages: Devil's Due for the Demon along with her Arcana and Thralls, while the Demonhounds are modified into homebrew fomori, the Succubus and the Imp are reworked into homebrew Banes, Umbrood or Bygones from the templates in Vampire: The Dark Ages. The Baali thrall is a follower of the Path of Cruelty, the Demonic Boar uses the Giant Boar template from Book of Storyteller Secrets modified with the Armor and Rapid Healing powers in the Bygone Bestiary to indicate that it's a Bygone created by the Demon. The land surrounding the village is also infested with dangerous demonic plants such as thorny vines and carnivorous plants.<br /> <br /> The Demon's true form is a cat-eyed satyr-like monstrosity. If you want, you could add a Hollow Woman fomor filled with venomous snakes and maybe a few other Celtic fomori? Maybe you could also add a Basilisk (Book of Storyteller Secrets) and a Cockatrice (Bygone Bestiary) as Bygones living in caves nearby?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-04-2024, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T01:50:49-07:00","id":1545203,"title":"","content":"There are, I think a few issues with this:<ul><li>So, we have a demon, plus demonhounds, plus a demonic boar, plus a Baali, plus a Black Spiral Dancer, plus a demonologist, plus an imp. This is far too much in thematic terms, even before you add basilisks and cockatrices. Generally, it's good to limit extraordinary villains to one per chronicle, otherwise individual antagonists just blend into the background.</li> <li>The next problem is that we have a demon ruling an lust cult in an isolated settlement in Scotland and the question is ... why? An isolated settlement might have, maybe, a hundred people. What's in it for her? What's in it for the player characters? (If I was a player in this chronicle, I would be noping out of there very quickly.)</li> <li>And there's no sense of the protagonists; what kind of characters would be drawn into this here? I could see something like this working as a <i>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</i> game, but it wouldn't necessarily fit with other games in the Dark Ages line.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T10:43:04-07:00","id":1545214,"title":"","content":"The reason it's isolated is so the cult won't be discovered easily while the Demon amasses power with it's Openly Demonic Cult and this is for a single story, not the entire chronicle. I was just going off of ideas and suggestions presented in the books. The protagonists could be a coterie of Kindred, a pack of Werewolves, a coven of Mages or a band of Inquisitors and it could work as long as the Storyteller is familiar with the rules of each game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-04-2024, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T18:26:47-08:00","id":1545359,"title":"","content":"One thing that I like to do is to have the Big Bad Boss being very close to the players. I once made a full story for a Fantasy game (using another system), where the players went from Zeroes to Heroes, starting from a small and unimportant village - I even made an entire fantasy industry related to oozes, you know, the D&amp;D type, oozes that dissolve, or rather &quot;digest&quot; the things they envelop, but this civilization discovered how to &quot;tame&quot; them, ending up using versions of oozes as toothpaste for instance, or sanitizers. Anyway, the players grew in this &quot;ooze farm&quot; village, until one day it got attacked by goblins, and hence their heroes journey begins. And you all know that no heroes journey is complete with your Gandalf, without your Obi wan Kenobi. Even Hercules had Chiron the Centaur as a mentor. The wise and ancient Paragon that guides the hero into their first steps.<br /> <br /> But here's the twist: my players &quot;Paragon&quot; Mentor was in fact the big final villain all along, manipulating them to his nefarious plans. He shows up during the attack, revealing that the &quot;old crazy Ben Kenobi&quot; was in fact a retired &quot;low tier wizard&quot; (he was in fact an arch master, but he didn't show that to them), and he guides the players into the defense of the village. Throughout the story, he will be the one holding their strings as a puppeteer.<br /> <br /> One thing you could do is introduce a Demonologist &quot;Demon Hunter&quot; as a &quot;mentor&quot; to the party, this being the one that will guide the party to deal with this &quot;dangerous succubus&quot; - and possibly many other devils along the way.<br /> <br /> The thing is thou, this &quot;demon hunter&quot; is actually a Nefandus Mage. Maybe he uses the role of &quot;Demon Hunter&quot; to recruit victims, and possibly he also REALLY hunts demons for the pragmatic reason of &quot;removing the competition&quot;. So, it serves two simultaneous purposes.<br /> <br /> That is one hell of an enemy, much more than the &quot;monster of the week&quot; that only exists basically for being vanquished by the players. This sort of antagonist, one that will become a &quot;friend&quot; of the party, is the kind that can utterly damn them.<br /> <br /> Just be careful how to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T12:13:05-08:00","id":1545400,"title":"","content":"So, you've done that in D&amp;D?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T07:36:35-08:00","id":1545935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1545400#post1545400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you've done that in D&amp;D?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me? Who are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T07:39:53-08:00","id":1545936,"title":"","content":"yes, I was referring to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T13:25:33-08:00","id":1546154,"title":"","content":"Since you're not responding, I'm going to say possible ways to begin said story. Maybe you first meet the Succubus when she attempts to seduce a member of your group, or maybe you're sent to investigate rumours of demonic activity somewhere in the Scottish Highlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-04-2024, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T14:14:42-08:00","id":1546602,"title":"","content":"Hello? Maximus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T08:53:10-08:00","id":1546644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1545936#post1545936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes, I was referring to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol oh ok, sorry. Yes, it was a D&amp;D campaign. I had the Big Bad Evil being the players mentor, for him to have his big reveal at the very end, after all their actions lead to a revolt against the king and plunging the realm into chaos.<br /> <br /> It was fun.<br /> <br /> For me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T09:07:25-08:00","id":1546645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1546602#post1546602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello? Maximus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry mate, I'm sorry. You know, place the Succubus as a &quot;lady in distress&quot; for the valiant heroes to rescue. Go slow, don't just go &quot;seduction route&quot; full on - the secret for &quot;demonic corruption&quot; is taking baby steps, each one ever closer to the abyss, and to initially appear as an angel of light. Portray her as an innocent and full of purity soul, have her play the role of a courtesan embroiled in some conspiracy against some really bad people, thus placing her in the position of victim needing help but also as someone who is resourceful, that can make things roll. You'll want to place her as the &quot;quest giver&quot;, so that she can have the role as the hand guiding the players actions. After that, she'll present the players with ever more morally questionable decisions they have to make - but also make sure that there are actually terrible consequences should they decide to go the &quot;moral high ground&quot; route and decide to &quot;do the right thing&quot;. For instance, say that she begs a player to kill the teenager son of the Baron, but being the heroes the players are, they refuse, only for this same teenager decree the death of one the helpless succubus &quot;daughters&quot; he was helping in captivity.<br /> <br /> After those initial stages, then she can start playing the &quot;seduction&quot; part, but always in tiny steps. &quot;Oh my hero, what would I do without you? I think... I think I have feelings for you, feelings I can no longer hold in my chest alone... If only I could do as my heart says, rather than what it is my obligation! I'm trapped into this loveless marriage with the Count, but my heart belongs to you fully... What shall I do now? Boo hoo boo hoo...&quot; And so on. Keep that up, until some (or preferably all the table) ends up in bed with her, but make sure the players keep it a secret from each other.<br /> <br /> Then amplify things a notch, with ever more cruel requests (for the greater good of course), until the players are no better than demons themselves, upon which she can have her grand reveal, ask for their souls directly and state &quot;you belong to Hell already dear. Now, the only thing you have to decide is if you either wish to rule in it, or be ruled. Your choice&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: and remember, the road to Hell is paved with good intentions. The greatest atrocities in human history were always done on behalf of the &quot;Greater Good&quot;. The USSR, Maoist China and even the Nazi Germany - Hitler saw himself as the hero of his own tale, and the nazis believed they were &quot;saving the world&quot;. Thus, the path of corruption always goes towards striving to achieve the &quot;greater good&quot;, particularly when you need to FORCE others to comply to YOUR (ours) ideas of &quot;good&quot;. That's why revolutions almost invariably end up in tyranny, when they are made based on some idea of social engineering society into what the revolutionaries believe to be the &quot;ideal society&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-05-2024, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T09:48:44-08:00","id":1546647,"title":"","content":"Well, considering the succubus is the recruiter for the other Demon that leads the Cult who is a Tempter. I was thinking whether they uncover the Succubus' true identity or not the story path leads one way or another to the village where the rest of the cult is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-29-2024, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T09:56:48-08:00","id":1546649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1546647#post1546647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, considering the succubus is the recruiter for the other Demon that leads the Cult who is an Enticer. I was thinking whether they uncover the Succubus' true identity or not the story path leads one way or another to the village where the rest of the cult is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so that's good. The Succubus can then let the village be sacrificed, literally thrown under the metaphorical bus (a literal metaphor, that's nice), so that she can play the role of the helpless victim of said cult. Or her master could do the same to her if you will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T10:09:28-08:00","id":1546650,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sounds good. The plot thickens in the village definitely. And in the case where the story starts another way where the party is sent by an authority figure to investigate possible demonic activity, chances are they might encounter the Cockatrice, Basilisk or Fomori first or maybe a Wyvern. Then after dealing with that they might be misled into thinking that, that was the source of the reports and the problem was dealt with when in reality they didn't find the root of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-05-2024, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T11:51:46-08:00","id":1546698,"title":"","content":"So, what did you think of that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T19:42:18-08:00","id":1546714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1546698#post1546698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what did you think of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good. Then you place the Succubus at the role of the &quot;virgin about to be sacrificed to Satan&quot; and your story is set to go. She then can get close to the players and get all sorts of shenanigans done. Make her to be someone of importance in the village - or better yet, you could have the entire village be part of the &quot;satanic cult&quot;. Sure, the villagers are oh, so thankful to the brave adventurers... Or so, it seems. In fact, that village is a hellish trap, waiting to sprung upon any would be 'saviors'.<br /> <br /> After that, you're set to go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T18:58:29-08:00","id":1546782,"title":"","content":"I always pictured a demon, during the Middle-Ages, really, perturbed that the Roman-Empire fell and Medieval-times was sort of a depressing, post-apocalyptic version of Europe for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T12:03:58-08:00","id":1546872,"title":"","content":"Well, the sources about Demons in the Dark Ages line give plenty of suggestions on how Demons view the World during that era. I just used the suggestions provided in Vampire: The Dark Ages and Dark Ages: Devil's Due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-11-2024, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T09:15:19-08:00","id":1547261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545084-concept-for-a-dark-ages-story-antagonist?p=1546714#post1546714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's good. Then you place the Succubus at the role of the &quot;virgin about to be sacrificed to Satan&quot; and your story is set to go. She then can get close to the players and get all sorts of shenanigans done. Make her to be someone of importance in the village - or better yet, you could have the entire village be part of the &quot;satanic cult&quot;. Sure, the villagers are oh, so thankful to the brave adventurers... Or so, it seems. In fact, that village is a hellish trap, waiting to sprung upon any would be 'saviors'.<br /> <br /> After that, you're set to go</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was thinking more along the lines of the Party thinking their work is done and leaving only for the Cult's influence to spread even further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T17:39:24-08:00","id":1547322,"title":"","content":"Maybe if the problem is ignored long enough then Dia's Demonologist summons another Tempter Demon such as Marbas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}